WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.468
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:08.738 --> 00:11.366
Arnold Swan chocolate.

3
00:11.449 --> 00:13.952
A treat from the Managing Partner for everyone.

4
00:15.453 --> 00:16.913
Thank you, Managing Partner.

5
00:19.999 --> 00:21.918
-Those cost 2,000 yen each. -2,000 yen?

6
00:22.001 --> 00:25.588
You don't have to hold back. This is a reward.

7
00:25.672 --> 00:27.757
It's thanks to your hard work, Ms. Minamida.

8
00:27.841 --> 00:30.301
Yes, it's thanks to Ms. Minamida's hard work.

9
00:30.385 --> 00:33.012
Hard workers must be properly rewarded.

10
00:33.096 --> 00:34.722
Keep up the good work!

11
00:39.769 --> 00:43.022
The Managing Partner is really soft on Ms. Minamida.

12
00:44.148 --> 00:47.235
And? The person in question isn't eating the reward?

13
00:47.819 --> 00:50.572
If it's a reward, I prefer the Minami Minamida set.

14
00:50.655 --> 00:52.282
Minami Minamida set?

15
00:52.365 --> 00:56.035
A set of three salted rice balls and sides my dad makes.

16
00:56.119 --> 00:58.079
But I don't really eat the sides.

17
00:58.830 --> 01:04.627
You can request that Minami Minamida set from the Managing Partner next time.

18
01:06.379 --> 01:08.798
If you want to eat the Minami Minamida set,

19
01:08.882 --> 01:10.675
you should come over to eat, Minato.

20
01:12.302 --> 01:14.053
-I'd like that. -Huh?

21
01:14.679 --> 01:16.097
You're calling him Minato now?

22
01:16.890 --> 01:18.975
Ah, there you are, Ms. Minamida.

23
01:20.518 --> 01:22.520
I have something to consult you about.

24
01:27.400 --> 01:29.444
I'm thinking of having you co-handle

25
01:29.527 --> 01:31.654
a case I'm taking on next.

26
01:32.155 --> 01:33.907
Have you heard of Fukamachi Biotech?

27
01:33.990 --> 01:36.701
They handle genetic engineering products.

28
01:36.784 --> 01:39.203
Fukamachi Biotech. I've heard of them.

29
01:39.287 --> 01:41.706
They're an old client,

30
01:41.789 --> 01:44.500
but the Chairman recently suffered a tragedy.

31
01:45.335 --> 01:48.129
His eldest son passed away.

32
01:49.172 --> 01:53.259
It seems his younger brother, who is a year younger, beat him to death.

33
01:56.012 --> 01:57.722
I'm so tired…

34
02:01.226 --> 02:02.101
So-chan?

35
02:02.769 --> 02:03.645
Sosuke?

36
02:03.728 --> 02:04.812
Sosuke?

37
02:05.313 --> 02:06.773
-Stop it! -So-chan?!

38
02:06.856 --> 02:08.233
-So-chan?! -Stop it!

39
02:09.192 --> 02:10.568
-No! Why? -Stop it!

40
02:10.652 --> 02:12.612
-Sosuke, calm down! -Stop it!

41
02:12.695 --> 02:15.281
-Calm down! -Stop it! Stop it!

42
02:17.200 --> 02:18.243
So-chan!

43
02:18.326 --> 02:20.328
-It's okay, you're okay now! -Shunsuke?

44
02:20.411 --> 02:22.080
-Sosuke, you're okay! -Shunsuke!

45
02:22.163 --> 02:23.998
Dear, what do we do! Shunsuke is…!

46
02:24.082 --> 02:25.541
What do we do? Shunsuke!

47
02:25.625 --> 02:27.502
Shunsuke? Shunsuke!

48
02:27.585 --> 02:29.295
-Stop it! -Shunsuke!

49
02:29.379 --> 02:31.798
I said stop it!

50
02:32.715 --> 02:36.844
The brother who committed the assault has autism.

51
02:36.928 --> 02:37.762
Yes.

52
02:41.182 --> 02:43.893
The older brother was rushed to the hospital unconscious,

53
02:43.977 --> 02:46.938
and died after being in a coma for a week.

54
02:47.021 --> 02:48.106
The cause of death

55
02:48.189 --> 02:50.650
was chest trauma causing internal bleeding

56
02:50.733 --> 02:53.486
in the chest cavity from 22 broken ribs.

57
02:54.278 --> 02:57.615
Were all these caused by his brother's assault?

58
02:57.699 --> 02:58.950
The prosecution thinks so.

59
02:59.617 --> 03:01.244
The fractures on the front of his ribs

60
03:01.327 --> 03:04.747
could have been caused by paramedics performing CPR.

61
03:04.831 --> 03:06.332
Even so…

62
03:06.916 --> 03:11.796
the victim also has 11 rib fractures on his back in a straight line.

63
03:11.879 --> 03:13.673
CPR doesn't explain that.

64
03:15.508 --> 03:18.344
Why would his brother do something like that?

65
03:19.512 --> 03:22.223
Apparently, when asked for a motive,

66
03:22.724 --> 03:25.768
he only says, "Stop it, stop it."

67
03:25.852 --> 03:27.812
"Stop it, stop it."

68
03:27.895 --> 03:30.815
The Chairman's family is coming shortly,

69
03:30.898 --> 03:32.316
so I want you to meet them.

70
03:32.400 --> 03:33.234
Yes.

71
03:39.782 --> 03:41.242
Thank you for having us.

72
03:41.326 --> 03:42.577
Thank you for coming.

73
03:45.413 --> 03:47.165
-Come in, So-chan. -Come in.

74
03:55.048 --> 03:55.965
Ultraman!

75
03:57.258 --> 03:58.801
You must like Ultraman.

76
04:01.596 --> 04:04.349
It's Ultraman Zero. Not just Ultraman.

77
04:04.432 --> 04:05.433
Zero!

78
04:06.225 --> 04:07.435
Please have a seat.

79
04:07.935 --> 04:08.770
So-chan.

80
04:10.980 --> 04:12.231
So-chan, sit here.

81
04:12.315 --> 04:13.483
Sit here.

82
04:16.486 --> 04:18.529
Take off your headphones and sunglasses.

83
04:18.613 --> 04:20.198
I don't want to.

84
04:20.907 --> 04:22.033
Listen.

85
04:22.617 --> 04:23.659
We made a promise, right?

86
04:23.743 --> 04:25.828
Listen. We didn't make a promise.

87
04:25.912 --> 04:27.538
We don't mind.

88
04:27.622 --> 04:29.082
Thank you for understanding.

89
04:31.084 --> 04:32.251
Sosuke.

90
04:32.960 --> 04:34.045
Hello.

91
04:34.545 --> 04:36.589
My name is Mr. Miyaji.

92
04:36.672 --> 04:40.134
-And this lady right here is… -Minami Minamida.

93
04:40.218 --> 04:43.471
My name is Minami Minamida, both forwards and backwards.

94
04:43.554 --> 04:45.473
Kayak, radar, civic, tacocat, racecar,

95
04:45.556 --> 04:46.974
Minami Minamida.

96
04:48.101 --> 04:51.020
Actually, Ms. Minamida also has autism.

97
04:54.690 --> 04:56.943
A lawyer with autism?

98
04:57.026 --> 04:59.821
We thought she could help defend your younger son,

99
04:59.904 --> 05:02.156
so we decided to have her co-handle the case.

100
05:02.240 --> 05:03.491
I see.

101
05:04.409 --> 05:05.743
Thank you very much.

102
05:06.911 --> 05:08.579
Yes, thank you very much.

103
05:08.663 --> 05:10.623
Yes, thank you very much.

104
05:12.083 --> 05:14.627
This lady and I

105
05:14.710 --> 05:17.505
have a whole lot of questions for you.

106
05:17.588 --> 05:19.507
So, today…

107
05:21.509 --> 05:22.510
What could that mean?

108
05:22.593 --> 05:23.928
I don't know.

109
05:26.681 --> 05:28.224
What's that?

110
05:30.017 --> 05:31.310
So-chan.

111
05:31.394 --> 05:32.854
So-chan, stop.

112
05:33.813 --> 05:34.730
Stop.

113
05:37.525 --> 05:41.779
Does your younger son usually get violent like this?

114
05:42.363 --> 05:43.239
No.

115
05:43.865 --> 05:46.534
He's easily misunderstood, but he's a very gentle boy.

116
05:46.617 --> 05:48.911
-Zero. -He would never attack anyone…

117
05:48.995 --> 05:49.996
Zero.

118
05:50.079 --> 05:52.707
Our eldest son also doted on him.

119
05:52.790 --> 05:54.625
They got along very well.

120
05:54.709 --> 06:00.047
So you have no idea what caused the assault, then.

121
06:00.131 --> 06:01.632
Even though he's my own child…

122
06:02.800 --> 06:04.343
I have no idea.

123
06:07.346 --> 06:08.556
Sosuke.

124
06:08.639 --> 06:11.601
Do you remember the day your older brother died?

125
06:14.770 --> 06:16.606
Why did you hit him?

126
06:16.689 --> 06:18.649
Did your brother do something to you?

127
06:18.733 --> 06:20.109
Slow down.

128
06:20.193 --> 06:24.322
Like, did he forcefully take your Ultraman Zero toy--

129
06:27.158 --> 06:29.285
So-chan, stop!

130
06:30.369 --> 06:31.662
-Sosuke! -So-chan!

131
06:31.746 --> 06:32.955
Calm down.

132
06:33.039 --> 06:36.000
-So-chan! -He gets like this when overstimulated.

133
06:36.542 --> 06:39.337
-Sosuke! It's okay. -So-chan…

134
06:52.850 --> 06:53.768
I'm home.

135
06:55.019 --> 06:57.647
Welcome home, Counselor.

136
06:59.440 --> 07:01.359
I have a question for you, Dad.

137
07:02.318 --> 07:03.236
A question?

138
07:04.820 --> 07:06.239
Okay.

139
07:09.867 --> 07:11.827
What's your question?

140
07:13.579 --> 07:17.500
Do people with autism ever get violent for no reason?

141
07:19.460 --> 07:23.256
You're the only autistic person I know, Minami.

142
07:23.339 --> 07:27.009
As for anyone else, you'd have to ask them directly to know for sure.

143
07:27.635 --> 07:31.556
He has severe autism with a mental age of 6 or 7,

144
07:31.639 --> 07:33.349
so he won't answer even if I ask.

145
07:33.975 --> 07:36.143
Then it might be tough.

146
07:37.228 --> 07:40.856
Dealing with someone with autism is lonely.

147
07:41.983 --> 07:42.858
Lonely?

148
07:43.818 --> 07:45.444
We're just a family of two,

149
07:45.987 --> 07:48.489
but you have absolutely no interest in me.

150
07:50.283 --> 07:52.994
I change my glasses, and you don't even mention it.

151
07:54.036 --> 07:55.621
It was even worse

152
07:55.705 --> 07:57.707
when you were a kid.

153
08:11.012 --> 08:14.390
Minami, I missed a step on the stairs…

154
08:15.474 --> 08:17.893
Look, my forehead. I scraped it.

155
08:17.977 --> 08:20.688
And my foot… I think I sprained it…

156
08:25.610 --> 08:26.527
It hurts…

157
08:36.162 --> 08:37.288
Blocks…

158
08:41.626 --> 08:44.170
Doesn't he have something he likes?

159
08:44.670 --> 08:46.631
If you want to get answers out of him,

160
08:46.714 --> 08:49.175
you should dig into what he likes.

161
08:49.759 --> 08:51.052
You have things you like too.

162
08:51.927 --> 08:53.763
I do have things I like. Whales!

163
08:54.263 --> 08:59.685
I was saved by your love of whales quite a bit.

164
09:02.271 --> 09:04.357
Does something hurt? Are you okay?

165
09:10.154 --> 09:11.781
Excuse me! Let me through.

166
09:11.864 --> 09:13.949
Minami! It's okay, it's Dad.

167
09:14.033 --> 09:16.202
I'm sorry. All right, let's go.

168
09:27.171 --> 09:28.130
My, my.

169
09:28.631 --> 09:30.091
Minami Minamida.

170
09:32.134 --> 09:35.805
Are you sleeping flipped over in a place like this?

171
09:38.599 --> 09:40.059
Sperm whales…

172
09:41.268 --> 09:45.231
sleep vertically in the water.

173
09:50.277 --> 09:51.737
You're good at sleeping standing up.

174
09:52.321 --> 09:53.406
Now,

175
09:53.489 --> 09:57.076
shall we migrate to the Sea of Okhotsk?

176
09:58.202 --> 09:59.036
I apologize.

177
10:00.079 --> 10:01.330
I am so very sorry.

178
10:01.831 --> 10:03.666
Let's go, Minami Minamida.

179
10:07.002 --> 10:10.131
Well, it'll take a lot of patience.

180
10:11.424 --> 10:15.177
But that's what communication is all about.

181
10:25.688 --> 10:27.481
Do I really have to do this?

182
10:27.565 --> 10:28.607
You have to do it.

183
10:28.691 --> 10:29.942
Excuse us.

184
10:34.530 --> 10:37.241
Hello, Sosuke!

185
10:37.324 --> 10:39.326
A special guest has come

186
10:39.410 --> 10:41.495
to see you today, Sosuke!

187
10:41.579 --> 10:42.747
Sit there.

188
10:45.958 --> 10:47.001
Please, have a seat.

189
10:50.504 --> 10:51.505
So-chan, over here.

190
10:51.589 --> 10:52.423
Over here?

191
10:53.174 --> 10:54.717
Sit here.

192
10:54.800 --> 10:56.093
Sit here.

193
11:00.139 --> 11:03.642
Now, please welcome our special guest!

194
11:06.937 --> 11:08.731
I am Zero!

195
11:08.814 --> 11:10.816
Ultraman Zero!

196
11:11.484 --> 11:16.989
Wow, Ultraman Zero has come to see you, Sosuke!

197
11:27.291 --> 11:28.375
Look out!

198
12:07.122 --> 12:10.042
All right, let's all call Zero's name

199
12:10.125 --> 12:11.752
and send him power!

200
12:11.835 --> 12:13.379
Ready, go!

201
12:17.174 --> 12:20.803
Let's all call Zero's name and send him power!

202
12:20.886 --> 12:22.513
-Ready, go! -What are they doing?

203
12:22.596 --> 12:26.475
She says it's a strategy to get the client to open up.

204
12:26.559 --> 12:29.311
Go, Ultraman Zero!

205
12:42.491 --> 12:43.534
It's not working…

206
12:54.169 --> 12:57.214
Mr. Miyaji, use your beam! Um, the Wide Zero Shot!

207
13:07.850 --> 13:09.059
You got me!

208
13:13.272 --> 13:14.565
You're 20,000 years too early!

209
13:16.942 --> 13:18.235
He seems to like it.

210
13:18.319 --> 13:19.862
Play! Zero!

211
13:19.945 --> 13:20.863
-Play! -Sosuke…

212
13:20.946 --> 13:22.072
We'll do it one more time.

213
13:22.156 --> 13:22.990
Yes, do it!

214
13:23.073 --> 13:24.533
Zero! Do it!

215
13:24.617 --> 13:26.827
No. We'll play Ultraman Zero

216
13:26.910 --> 13:29.538
after you answer our questions.

217
13:29.622 --> 13:31.457
-Zero! -First, please answer.

218
13:31.957 --> 13:33.667
Why did you hit your brother?

219
13:39.506 --> 13:40.924
Ms. Minamida, let's call it here.

220
13:41.508 --> 13:43.093
Please answer.

221
13:43.177 --> 13:45.095
What did your brother do to you?

222
13:45.179 --> 13:47.056
Stop it!

223
13:47.139 --> 13:49.808
-Stop it! -It's okay, So-chan.

224
13:50.392 --> 13:53.896
I'm sorry. It might be impossible for him to answer questions after all.

225
13:53.979 --> 13:56.523
-And it was going so well, too. -So-chan, stop.

226
13:56.607 --> 14:00.778
-Stop it! -So-chan, it's okay.

227
14:03.614 --> 14:07.493
The police have finished investigating the older brother's room, right?

228
14:07.576 --> 14:09.662
Will we find anything if we search it now?

229
14:10.162 --> 14:11.330
On-site police investigation

230
14:11.413 --> 14:13.916
was for suspicion of assault,

231
14:13.999 --> 14:15.876
not murder or manslaughter.

232
14:15.959 --> 14:18.712
The investigation might not have been thorough.

233
14:18.796 --> 14:20.172
I see.

234
14:22.800 --> 14:24.093
Funai?

235
14:24.927 --> 14:26.011
Long time no see!

236
14:26.971 --> 14:29.306
Oh, do you live around here?

237
14:29.390 --> 14:30.766
No, I'm here for work.

238
14:31.350 --> 14:32.184
Oh, I see.

239
14:32.267 --> 14:33.560
What work?

240
14:41.986 --> 14:44.738
Are you still doing that volunteer work for the disabled?

241
14:44.822 --> 14:46.156
It's not like that.

242
14:47.157 --> 14:50.035
We have to go, or we'll be late. Let's go.

243
14:51.745 --> 14:52.913
See you.

244
14:52.997 --> 14:53.831
Yeah.

245
14:57.042 --> 15:00.838
Um, that was a classmate from college. Sorry about what she said.

246
15:00.921 --> 15:01.922
It's fine.

247
15:06.385 --> 15:08.345
Everything has been left as it was.

248
15:08.846 --> 15:10.180
Let me know when you're done.

249
15:10.264 --> 15:11.098
Thank you.

250
15:30.075 --> 15:32.202
When the parents came home,

251
15:32.286 --> 15:34.288
Sosuke was straddling his older brother

252
15:34.371 --> 15:36.957
right under this beam and hitting him, right?

253
15:40.836 --> 15:42.921
With his back to the entrance. So…

254
15:45.007 --> 15:45.883
Like this?

255
15:46.383 --> 15:47.217
Yes.

256
15:47.968 --> 15:49.136
If that's the case,

257
15:51.013 --> 15:53.182
the older brother would be like this.

258
15:53.682 --> 15:54.850
That's right.

259
15:57.728 --> 15:58.979
What happened

260
15:59.480 --> 16:01.231
between them before this?

261
16:01.315 --> 16:03.609
The reason for "Stop it, stop it," right.

262
16:14.036 --> 16:16.580
Minato, please play the role of the older brother.

263
16:18.207 --> 16:21.960
For example, they fought over the Ultraman Zero toy.

264
16:25.047 --> 16:26.799
Let me borrow that Zero for a bit.

265
16:28.092 --> 16:30.552
Stop it! Stop it!

266
16:30.636 --> 16:31.762
Stop it!

267
16:31.845 --> 16:32.930
Stop it!

268
16:35.682 --> 16:36.600
I'll grab it.

269
16:41.063 --> 16:42.981
Sorry, this was in front of it.

270
16:49.488 --> 16:50.531
I got it.

271
16:51.990 --> 16:53.117
Ms. Minamida?

272
16:53.200 --> 16:56.286
This electrical cord is bent in two places.

273
16:56.370 --> 16:59.206
As if some heavy tension was applied to it.

274
17:04.128 --> 17:07.589
This width is exactly the same size as that beam.

275
17:07.673 --> 17:09.383
Can I take it for a moment?

276
17:14.054 --> 17:15.389
The death certificate

277
17:15.472 --> 17:19.184
mentions some kind of mark left on the victim's neck.

278
17:19.810 --> 17:23.021
Was the older brother trying to hang himself with this?

279
17:29.695 --> 17:30.696
I see!

280
17:30.779 --> 17:33.282
Sosuke's "Stop it, stop it"

281
17:33.365 --> 17:35.200
wasn't because his brother hurt him.

282
17:35.284 --> 17:38.036
He was trying to stop his brother's actions.

283
17:44.376 --> 17:45.919
Stop it!

284
17:47.713 --> 17:49.882
Stop it!

285
17:50.465 --> 17:51.967
Stop it!

286
17:52.718 --> 17:55.762
There might be other clues left behind.

287
18:02.644 --> 18:03.478
What's this?

288
18:03.562 --> 18:06.481
This is Shunsuke's notebook that was left in his room.

289
18:13.197 --> 18:15.240
It seems your eldest son wrote

290
18:15.324 --> 18:16.450
his thoughts

291
18:16.533 --> 18:19.703
and words of encouragement in this notebook between study sessions.

292
18:22.372 --> 18:25.042
We believe these are recent entries.

293
18:26.210 --> 18:28.462
Please look at the last page he wrote.

294
18:34.968 --> 18:37.763
I CAN'T SEE THE END. I JUST WANT TO ESCAPE.

295
18:42.142 --> 18:43.101
It's too hard.

296
18:45.520 --> 18:48.440
If I don't try harder, I'll be left behind.

297
18:52.194 --> 18:54.696
The exams will keep coming,

298
18:55.447 --> 18:58.283
and I'll fail again.

299
19:01.161 --> 19:02.204
I guess

300
19:03.163 --> 19:04.623
dying is the only way out.

301
19:07.251 --> 19:08.585
The only way out…

302
19:12.047 --> 19:14.216
Is it possible

303
19:14.299 --> 19:16.885
your eldest son was trying to commit suicide that day?

304
19:17.427 --> 19:20.138
This electrical cord was in his room.

305
19:20.639 --> 19:23.809
We believe he may have been trying to hang himself with it.

306
19:25.102 --> 19:28.272
Sosuke must have happened to see it.

307
19:28.730 --> 19:32.192
And Sosuke must have gotten violent

308
19:32.276 --> 19:34.987
because he couldn't bear to see his beloved older brother

309
19:35.070 --> 19:36.321
trying to take his own life.

310
19:36.405 --> 19:38.699
-And that caused him to panic… -Shunsuke…

311
19:39.783 --> 19:40.784
would never kill himself.

312
19:40.867 --> 19:42.035
But…

313
19:42.119 --> 19:45.247
Everyone vents their feelings in a diary or online

314
19:45.330 --> 19:46.665
when they're struggling, right?

315
19:52.879 --> 19:53.797
Sosuke.

316
20:02.431 --> 20:03.932
Did you see

317
20:04.599 --> 20:08.854
your older brother trying to kill himself that day?

318
20:10.605 --> 20:11.440
Yes.

319
20:16.695 --> 20:17.529
That's impossible.

320
20:18.363 --> 20:20.532
Huh? But he just said "Yes."

321
20:28.832 --> 20:29.916
So-chan.

322
20:32.044 --> 20:33.837
Did your brother try to kill himself?

323
20:36.256 --> 20:37.090
Yes.

324
20:38.050 --> 20:39.009
So-chan.

325
20:40.260 --> 20:42.262
Did your brother try to live?

326
20:43.096 --> 20:44.097
Yes.

327
20:44.931 --> 20:48.101
Your brother never tried to kill himself?

328
20:48.685 --> 20:49.519
Yes.

329
20:55.067 --> 20:57.194
Communicating in a way that matches his level

330
20:57.277 --> 20:59.946
is still difficult even for us.

331
21:02.282 --> 21:04.868
But if we examine this cord closely…

332
21:04.951 --> 21:07.079
There's no need for that.

333
21:08.663 --> 21:11.583
You don't have to disgrace our dead son.

334
21:13.585 --> 21:16.880
What about the honor of the son who's still alive?

335
21:17.464 --> 21:21.134
You must prove he didn't beat his brother to death for no reason

336
21:21.218 --> 21:22.719
-just because he has autism. -Shut up!

337
21:24.638 --> 21:26.056
You're autistic too, aren't you?

338
21:26.640 --> 21:27.849
Who do you think you are?

339
21:27.933 --> 21:28.975
Um…

340
21:31.103 --> 21:33.355
Please… just go home for today.

341
21:43.532 --> 21:44.658
What's up?

342
21:44.741 --> 21:46.451
I heard you made the client angry.

343
21:46.535 --> 21:48.036
Ah, yeah.

344
21:48.120 --> 21:50.622
You have to maneuver these things better.

345
21:51.540 --> 21:54.626
Well, I guess that's not easy with Ms. Minamida around.

346
21:56.753 --> 21:58.004
Anyway, I'm heading home.

347
22:02.551 --> 22:03.760
Have a good evening.

348
22:09.808 --> 22:13.019
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

349
22:15.480 --> 22:19.025
GREAT WORK TODAY. ALSO, ABOUT MY ACQUAINTANCE BEING RUDE EARLIER…

350
22:29.077 --> 22:31.496
What am I even trying to do by apologizing…

351
22:32.164 --> 22:34.249
In the case of the 23-year-old

352
22:34.332 --> 22:37.669
indicted for beating his older brother to death.

353
22:37.752 --> 22:42.340
Since the younger brother was diagnosed with autism,

354
22:42.424 --> 22:44.968
various opinions are circulating online.

355
22:45.051 --> 22:47.637
Of course, disability and crime

356
22:47.721 --> 22:50.473
are separate issues.

357
22:50.557 --> 22:53.143
However, considering this case…

358
22:59.774 --> 23:02.235
24-YEAR-OLD DIES AT HOME: AUTISTIC BROTHER ACCUSED OF ASSAULT

359
23:02.319 --> 23:05.697
IT'S A LOSS TO SOCIETY THAT A BRIGHT YOUNG MAN DIED INSTEAD OF THE DISABLED GUY

360
23:05.780 --> 23:08.491
HE'S DEFINITELY GOING TO THE PSYCH WARD

361
23:12.162 --> 23:14.247
IT CAN'T BE HELPED BECAUSE HE'S AUTISTIC

362
23:20.378 --> 23:23.632
THE PEOPLE AROUND HIM NEED TO TAKE RESPONSIBILITY AND SUPERVISE HIM

363
23:29.054 --> 23:32.140
IT'S SCARY. DON'T WE NEED MEASURES CLOSER TO ISOLATION?

364
23:42.442 --> 23:44.236
Hey, buddy.

365
23:44.319 --> 23:47.489
No! Don't just wander off!

366
23:47.572 --> 23:49.574
-No! -Hey, buddy.

367
23:49.658 --> 23:51.284
-You haven't paid the fare yet. -Sosuke?

368
23:52.285 --> 23:53.870
Hey, buddy. Hey?

369
23:54.579 --> 23:57.249
Hey? You haven't paid the fare yet.

370
23:57.749 --> 24:00.043
Buddy! Listen to me!

371
24:03.421 --> 24:04.256
What happened?

372
24:09.803 --> 24:10.637
Sosuke?

373
24:12.138 --> 24:14.015
-Hey! -Did something happen?

374
24:15.517 --> 24:16.476
Do you know him?

375
24:16.559 --> 24:17.560
Yes.

376
24:17.644 --> 24:20.146
This guy suddenly got in my taxi

377
24:20.230 --> 24:23.275
and said he was going to this law firm, so I brought him here.

378
24:23.358 --> 24:28.405
I told him the fare, but he started saying, "Zero, zero." I'm at a loss.

379
24:28.488 --> 24:29.406
I'll pay for him.

380
24:29.489 --> 24:30.407
Zero.

381
24:31.491 --> 24:33.285
Thank you. That helps a lot.

382
24:34.828 --> 24:36.413
Zero!

383
24:37.038 --> 24:38.790
Let's head inside the office for now.

384
24:38.873 --> 24:39.958
Okay.

385
24:42.168 --> 24:43.378
Sosuke.

386
24:43.878 --> 24:45.755
Belial is over there!

387
24:46.256 --> 24:48.466
What?! Belial! Okay!

388
24:49.050 --> 24:50.802
Who are you?

389
24:50.885 --> 24:52.679
My name is Zero!

390
24:52.762 --> 24:53.972
The son of Seven!

391
24:57.934 --> 24:59.102
Sosuke.

392
24:59.185 --> 25:01.062
Sosuke, can you attack me

393
25:01.146 --> 25:03.565
right here with the Big Bang Zero?

394
25:03.648 --> 25:05.275
-Right here. -They're here.

395
25:07.652 --> 25:08.737
So-chan.

396
25:10.613 --> 25:11.656
Mom!

397
25:15.201 --> 25:17.370
You can't just wander off on your own.

398
25:20.081 --> 25:23.043
I'm so sorry for the trouble he caused.

399
25:23.126 --> 25:24.794
I'm just glad nothing happened.

400
25:25.837 --> 25:26.838
Um…

401
25:27.589 --> 25:29.382
about my husband being rude the other day…

402
25:30.383 --> 25:31.885
Oh… no, it's fine.

403
25:32.719 --> 25:34.721
I shouldn't say this,

404
25:35.680 --> 25:37.182
but meeting you

405
25:37.974 --> 25:40.143
left my husband and me feeling conflicted.

406
25:41.478 --> 25:43.146
Even though you have the same autism,

407
25:43.229 --> 25:45.523
you're so different from our son.

408
25:47.984 --> 25:51.988
I want you all to handle this case.

409
25:55.241 --> 25:56.409
However…

410
25:57.702 --> 25:58.745
I would like to ask

411
26:00.789 --> 26:02.791
that you do so without revealing

412
26:03.291 --> 26:05.251
that Shunsuke made that kind of choice.

413
26:06.002 --> 26:06.836
Yes.

414
26:09.297 --> 26:12.217
We won't reveal anything that could dishonor your eldest son.

415
26:13.385 --> 26:14.636
Thank you.

416
26:22.852 --> 26:25.063
COURTHOUSE

417
26:29.818 --> 26:30.819
FIRST TRIAL: WITNESS EXAM

418
26:30.902 --> 26:32.529
I think the defendant panicked.

419
26:33.822 --> 26:36.533
What do you mean by panic?

420
26:37.117 --> 26:39.828
It's common in people with autism.

421
26:39.911 --> 26:42.372
Unable to withstand stress or sudden strong stimuli,

422
26:42.455 --> 26:45.625
they fall into a state of extreme confusion.

423
26:47.293 --> 26:48.128
So

424
26:48.962 --> 26:52.132
the defendant's action of hitting his brother

425
26:52.215 --> 26:55.552
occurred in a situation where it was difficult to control his own behavior.

426
26:56.261 --> 26:58.471
In other words, at the time,

427
26:58.555 --> 27:01.599
the defendant's ability to control his actions

428
27:01.683 --> 27:06.062
was diminished due to a panic commonly experienced by people with autism?

429
27:06.146 --> 27:07.856
I believe so.

430
27:10.817 --> 27:11.818
Nothing further.

431
27:13.945 --> 27:17.949
Witness, you are a psychiatrist specializing in autism, correct?

432
27:18.700 --> 27:20.118
Well… yes.

433
27:20.201 --> 27:21.035
In that case,

434
27:21.619 --> 27:25.331
can you tell us how many autistic people are in this courtroom right now?

435
27:26.875 --> 27:29.586
What about the attorney who questioned you?

436
27:29.669 --> 27:30.795
Objection.

437
27:31.504 --> 27:35.216
The prosecutor is insulting the defense with discriminatory remarks.

438
27:36.301 --> 27:37.135
Overruled.

439
27:37.844 --> 27:39.929
I understand your point,

440
27:40.013 --> 27:42.432
but I can't say it's completely irrelevant.

441
27:43.099 --> 27:45.143
Prosecutor, mind your phrasing.

442
27:45.226 --> 27:46.102
Yes, Your Honor.

443
27:47.312 --> 27:50.940
Does the defense attorney who just questioned you have autism?

444
27:55.361 --> 27:59.282
I've heard the attorney over there has autism.

445
27:59.365 --> 28:00.325
And do you believe

446
28:00.950 --> 28:02.785
the defendant had a diminished capacity

447
28:02.869 --> 28:06.372
to control his actions at the time of the crime?

448
28:06.456 --> 28:07.290
Yes.

449
28:07.373 --> 28:10.585
You claim diminished capacity because he has autism?

450
28:10.668 --> 28:11.503
Yes.

451
28:11.586 --> 28:12.420
But…

452
28:12.504 --> 28:15.048
Is the defense attorney also in a state of diminished capacity?

453
28:15.131 --> 28:15.965
Objection!

454
28:16.716 --> 28:19.928
The defense attorney's circumstances are irrelevant to the case.

455
28:20.011 --> 28:21.262
They're not irrelevant.

456
28:21.346 --> 28:25.517
The defense argues for leniency due to autism.

457
28:25.600 --> 28:28.228
If the defendant has diminished capacity due to autism,

458
28:28.311 --> 28:30.688
doesn't the defense attorney as well?

459
28:30.772 --> 28:32.315
Diminished capacity is judged

460
28:32.398 --> 28:34.859
based on the circumstances at the time of the crime.

461
28:34.943 --> 28:36.277
Autism

462
28:36.361 --> 28:39.739
doesn't automatically mean diminished capacity.

463
28:39.823 --> 28:44.619
You argue the autistic defendant deserves leniency,

464
28:44.702 --> 28:48.998
yet demand the autistic lawyer be treated equally to other lawyers?

465
28:49.082 --> 28:50.458
Isn't that strange?

466
28:50.542 --> 28:51.459
Prosecutor.

467
28:51.543 --> 28:56.506
I'm simply pointing out a contradiction in the defense's argument.

468
28:57.006 --> 28:58.383
Nothing further.

469
29:12.480 --> 29:14.983
That prosecutor's logic is completely absurd.

470
29:15.066 --> 29:19.195
He doesn't understand Autism Spectrum Disorder or diminished capacity at all.

471
29:19.279 --> 29:20.363
Mr. Miyaji.

472
29:20.446 --> 29:21.281
Yes.

473
29:22.323 --> 29:23.658
I'm sorry,

474
29:24.617 --> 29:28.872
but could you please take Ms. Minamida off the case going forward?

475
29:30.331 --> 29:33.585
Of course, I know she's worked hard for us.

476
29:34.085 --> 29:37.463
But when the prosecutor attacks us like that…

477
29:38.214 --> 29:41.175
That's just their strategy to shake us up.

478
29:42.010 --> 29:43.970
The defendant's diminished capacity

479
29:44.053 --> 29:46.890
won't be rejected just because his attorney has autism.

480
29:46.973 --> 29:49.017
That logic wouldn't hold up.

481
29:49.100 --> 29:50.184
Please understand.

482
29:50.268 --> 29:53.354
We must do what's best for Sosuke.

483
29:55.023 --> 29:58.401
I want to eliminate every possible disadvantage.

484
30:05.575 --> 30:07.243
I don't mind.

485
30:08.369 --> 30:10.997
Please take me off the case.

486
30:14.834 --> 30:16.502
I'm honestly frustrated.

487
30:16.586 --> 30:20.673
You were working so hard for the client, Ms. Minamida.

488
30:29.724 --> 30:30.850
I think

489
30:31.601 --> 30:33.186
the Chairman is right.

490
30:34.479 --> 30:36.022
How so?

491
30:37.231 --> 30:41.778
When people see you and me walking together,

492
30:42.820 --> 30:46.449
they think you're doing volunteer work for the disabled.

493
30:47.533 --> 30:49.786
Still doing that volunteer work for the disabled?

494
30:50.536 --> 30:53.414
When Sosuke didn't pay the taxi fare,

495
30:53.498 --> 30:54.624
the driver

496
30:55.833 --> 30:59.087
didn't think I could resolve the situation.

497
31:01.255 --> 31:05.551
I know how Sosuke and I are different

498
31:08.096 --> 31:10.056
even though we both have autism,

499
31:11.432 --> 31:13.851
but the prosecutor and the jury won't understand.

500
31:15.228 --> 31:16.854
That's why, I…

501
31:20.984 --> 31:22.735
I can't help…

502
31:27.824 --> 31:28.866
the defendant.

503
31:34.372 --> 31:35.707
In Nazi Germany,

504
31:36.457 --> 31:38.084
until 81 years ago,

505
31:38.584 --> 31:40.461
the rights of people with disabilities

506
31:40.545 --> 31:43.256
were stripped away through laws and government policies,

507
31:43.339 --> 31:47.260
and some were killed as lives "unworthy of life."

508
31:48.720 --> 31:49.679
People with

509
31:50.263 --> 31:53.474
Autism Spectrum Disorder were included among them.

510
32:02.275 --> 32:03.234
Let's go.

511
32:09.615 --> 32:11.325
Sosuke and I

512
32:11.951 --> 32:15.496
are people whose worthiness to live was once measured.

513
32:16.831 --> 32:18.624
And even now, many people

514
32:19.417 --> 32:23.755
press "Like" on comments saying it is a loss to society

515
32:23.838 --> 32:26.758
that a bright young man died instead of a disabled person.

516
32:28.051 --> 32:33.056
That's our reality with Autism Spectrum Disorder.

517
32:43.191 --> 32:44.692
Mr. Miyaji asked me

518
32:44.776 --> 32:46.778
to take over

519
32:46.861 --> 32:50.740
the Fukamachi Biotech case from Ms. Minamida.

520
32:50.823 --> 32:52.617
Oh, really.

521
32:52.700 --> 32:54.577
Well, I'll make sure the rest goes smoothly.

522
32:55.745 --> 32:58.873
Look forward to a treat from the Managing Partner.

523
33:03.920 --> 33:05.129
What a jerk.

524
33:18.643 --> 33:19.727
Ms. Minamida.

525
33:22.105 --> 33:23.064
I'm coming in.

526
33:25.691 --> 33:26.692
Ms. Minamida!

527
33:59.267 --> 34:02.520
Minato, your hand is firmly grabbing my butt.

528
34:04.313 --> 34:05.273
I'm sorry.

529
34:10.486 --> 34:13.281
Minato grabbed my butt.

530
34:13.364 --> 34:16.659
Minato grabbed my butt!

531
34:25.084 --> 34:26.836
It's because of the butt-grabbing!

532
34:26.919 --> 34:27.837
Um…

533
34:30.840 --> 34:32.341
Ms. Minamida! Your shoes!

534
34:35.761 --> 34:36.721
Come in.

535
34:36.804 --> 34:37.680
Excuse me.

536
34:42.727 --> 34:43.561
What is it?

537
34:43.644 --> 34:45.188
I was hanging myself earlier…

538
34:45.271 --> 34:46.939
…but Minato saved me.

539
34:47.023 --> 34:51.110
First, Minato used his left hand to lift my butt up like this.

540
34:51.194 --> 34:54.030
Then, he tried to remove the cord from my neck with his right hand.

541
34:54.113 --> 34:55.740
What do you think happened then?

542
34:55.823 --> 34:56.657
I have no idea.

543
34:56.741 --> 34:59.702
My body tilted back, and I fell on my back.

544
34:59.785 --> 35:00.620
What's this about?

545
35:01.495 --> 35:05.041
The brother's cause of death was internal bleeding from broken ribs.

546
35:05.124 --> 35:06.584
The death certificate

547
35:06.667 --> 35:09.587
stated 22 of his ribs were broken.

548
35:09.670 --> 35:13.341
Five right anterior ribs, numbers three through seven.

549
35:13.424 --> 35:16.802
Six left anterior ribs, two through seven.

550
35:16.886 --> 35:18.471
And on the back…

551
35:22.016 --> 35:24.435
um, let me borrow your ribs for a second.

552
35:24.518 --> 35:25.770
Yes, go ahead.

553
35:25.853 --> 35:26.854
11 right posterior ribs,

554
35:26.938 --> 35:29.857
numbers two through twelve.

555
35:29.941 --> 35:31.776
There were no fractures elsewhere.

556
35:31.859 --> 35:34.987
What's more, the 11 fractures in the right posterior ribs

557
35:35.071 --> 35:36.113
form a straight line.

558
35:36.197 --> 35:37.448
Isn't that strange?

559
35:39.033 --> 35:41.577
I heard that when Sosuke gets overstimulated,

560
35:41.661 --> 35:44.080
he keeps jumping up and down until he calms down.

561
35:44.872 --> 35:46.499
When in a state like that,

562
35:46.582 --> 35:49.085
I think it would be extremely difficult to punch

563
35:49.168 --> 35:51.796
his brother straight in the back so that the ribs

564
35:51.879 --> 35:53.547
break cleanly in a straight line.

565
35:54.131 --> 35:57.760
However, it is possible if Sosuke tried to save his older brother

566
35:57.843 --> 36:00.596
using the exact same method Minato did.

567
36:01.430 --> 36:04.976
Because the defendant firmly grabbed the victim's butt,

568
36:05.059 --> 36:07.395
the victim fell onto his back on the floor.

569
36:08.104 --> 36:10.273
Just like his beloved Ultraman Zero would,

570
36:10.356 --> 36:14.193
Sosuke must have been trying to protect his brother.

571
36:21.158 --> 36:22.076
An accident?

572
36:23.077 --> 36:23.911
Yes.

573
36:23.995 --> 36:27.498
The fractures may not have been caused by Sosuke's assault.

574
36:27.581 --> 36:29.917
And when Sosuke was straddling him,

575
36:30.001 --> 36:33.671
he might have just been trying to wake up your unconscious son.

576
36:34.755 --> 36:35.798
So Sosuke…

577
36:37.508 --> 36:40.219
was trying to save his brother.

578
36:44.390 --> 36:46.600
Assault charges may still be warranted,

579
36:46.684 --> 36:49.270
but we can clear him of suspicion of causing death by assault.

580
36:53.274 --> 36:54.275
However…

581
36:55.026 --> 36:56.152
to do that,

582
36:56.235 --> 37:00.364
we must reveal the fact that your eldest son attempted suicide.

583
37:02.450 --> 37:05.077
We'd like you to decide what to do, Chairman.

584
37:06.495 --> 37:07.330
Dear…

585
37:10.499 --> 37:11.792
When you get to this age,

586
37:13.461 --> 37:16.881
your children start to feel like a report card on your life.

587
37:18.049 --> 37:19.175
Partly because of that,

588
37:20.509 --> 37:22.428
honestly, I didn't want to admit

589
37:23.095 --> 37:26.057
that my eldest son was unhappy.

590
37:26.766 --> 37:27.683
But…

591
37:28.309 --> 37:30.436
I WANT TO BECOME RESPECTABLE LIKE MY PARENTS

592
37:30.519 --> 37:34.065
I TRIED SO HARD TO GET EVEN ONE STEP CLOSER TO THEM, SO WHY AM I LIKE THIS?

593
37:34.899 --> 37:35.858
He…

594
37:36.567 --> 37:39.528
had sensed those expectations of ours.

595
37:43.282 --> 37:44.742
We were the ones who pushed

596
37:45.493 --> 37:47.370
our son into a corner, weren't we?

597
37:48.371 --> 37:50.581
If he were alive,

598
37:52.333 --> 37:53.751
I'm sure

599
37:55.211 --> 37:56.504
he would tell us this:

600
37:59.382 --> 38:00.466
"Please protect…

601
38:03.886 --> 38:04.887
my little brother."

602
38:05.888 --> 38:07.390
"Protect Sosuke."

603
38:11.394 --> 38:12.478
Please

604
38:14.105 --> 38:15.689
take care of Sosuke.

605
38:17.191 --> 38:18.275
Understood.

606
38:22.613 --> 38:23.656
Regarding that…

607
38:24.532 --> 38:25.699
Yes.

608
38:25.783 --> 38:28.244
Ms. Minamida is the one who noticed

609
38:28.327 --> 38:30.037
this was an accident.

610
38:30.121 --> 38:32.415
-As for who handles the case… -That's…

611
38:37.586 --> 38:38.838
Ms. Minamida.

612
38:41.424 --> 38:42.591
Ms. Minamida.

613
38:44.135 --> 38:45.594
The meeting just ended.

614
38:46.387 --> 38:49.849
We're going to make his suicide attempt public

615
38:49.932 --> 38:52.184
and argue that his death was accidental.

616
38:53.769 --> 38:55.771
I see. I'm glad.

617
38:55.855 --> 38:56.689
Yeah.

618
38:57.398 --> 39:00.192
Oh, and about who's handling the case…

619
39:07.450 --> 39:09.493
I won't be of any help,

620
39:10.494 --> 39:13.414
so please handle it, Mr. Himi.

621
39:14.457 --> 39:16.167
Ah, right.

622
39:17.376 --> 39:18.419
Leave it to me.

623
39:43.152 --> 39:44.820
Please, right this way.

624
39:53.496 --> 39:54.830
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

625
39:54.914 --> 39:56.916
AREN'T YOU COMING TO OBSERVE THE 10 AM TRIAL?

626
40:03.881 --> 40:06.675
Minami, it's time to wake up. I'm opening the door.

627
40:12.056 --> 40:13.349
It's already 10:00.

628
40:13.432 --> 40:14.767
I can't wash your pajamas.

629
40:17.603 --> 40:18.896
Do you have the day off?

630
40:20.564 --> 40:21.857
I'll go later.

631
40:23.025 --> 40:24.109
It'll be noon soon.

632
40:34.620 --> 40:37.289
Now, will the defendant please take the stand.

633
40:39.583 --> 40:41.418
Sosuke, right this way.

634
40:42.002 --> 40:42.836
Yes.

635
40:44.547 --> 40:45.422
Sosuke!

636
40:47.258 --> 40:48.217
Right this way.

637
40:48.717 --> 40:49.552
Yes.

638
40:55.432 --> 40:58.227
Next is the defendant's questioning,

639
40:58.727 --> 41:03.023
but please allow me to ask him some questions first.

640
41:03.816 --> 41:04.900
Defendant.

641
41:06.569 --> 41:08.404
Sosuke Fukamachi.

642
41:09.697 --> 41:10.698
Yes.

643
41:11.198 --> 41:13.784
You heard the defense attorney's statement, right?

644
41:14.535 --> 41:17.830
Did you, the defendant, lower your brother to the floor?

645
41:20.416 --> 41:21.500
Yes.

646
41:23.252 --> 41:26.297
Did you try to save your brother?

647
41:28.882 --> 41:29.717
Yes!

648
41:29.800 --> 41:33.220
The electrical cord didn't just come off on its own.

649
41:33.304 --> 41:34.138
Yes…

650
41:35.389 --> 41:37.182
Please answer clearly.

651
41:37.266 --> 41:41.228
Was it you who lowered your brother? Or was it not?

652
41:49.028 --> 41:49.945
Yes!

653
42:00.205 --> 42:01.999
Sosuke Fukamachi.

654
42:02.082 --> 42:05.294
You tried to save your brother. Is that right?

655
42:05.377 --> 42:06.587
Or is it not?

656
42:26.899 --> 42:28.150
Yes!

657
42:38.744 --> 42:39.828
You did great.

658
42:40.829 --> 42:42.706
Well, we presented our argument,

659
42:42.790 --> 42:45.084
and the jury's reaction was good.

660
42:45.167 --> 42:48.671
I doubt he'll be convicted of causing death by assault.

661
42:48.754 --> 42:51.548
Even if he gets convicted of assault over the facial injuries,

662
42:51.632 --> 42:53.467
he'll probably get a suspended sentence.

663
42:53.967 --> 42:54.968
I'm so glad.

664
42:58.097 --> 42:59.556
Thank you very much.

665
43:00.182 --> 43:01.141
It's all thanks to you.

666
43:01.225 --> 43:02.101
Not at all.

667
43:03.394 --> 43:04.395
Things ended

668
43:04.478 --> 43:06.814
in an impolite manner this time,

669
43:07.356 --> 43:10.401
but I hope you'll pass on our thanks to Ms. Minamida as well.

670
43:10.484 --> 43:11.568
Understood.

671
43:11.652 --> 43:14.863
I imagine she's also wondering how the trial turned out.

672
43:14.947 --> 43:17.700
I'll contact Ms. Minamida myself.

673
43:17.783 --> 43:19.785
Please do.

674
43:20.994 --> 43:21.954
Let's go.

675
43:33.966 --> 43:35.050
You got me!

676
43:35.676 --> 43:36.510
You did it!

677
43:44.643 --> 43:45.936
-Then let's go. -Okay.

678
43:49.314 --> 43:51.650
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

679
44:45.788 --> 44:47.164
Ms. Minamida…

680
44:50.834 --> 44:55.839
Subtitle translation by: Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

681
44:56.548 --> 44:57.883
You should stay a lawyer.

682
44:57.966 --> 45:01.094
I think Ririi would be happy if you defended her.

683
45:01.178 --> 45:02.888
Can't we support her somehow?

684
45:02.971 --> 45:03.805
Unfortunately.

685
45:03.889 --> 45:05.682
I can't help Ririi.

686
45:05.766 --> 45:07.851
Going to court is an overreaction, isn't it?

687
45:07.935 --> 45:10.771
Because you've always swept things under the rug, it's come to this!

688
45:10.854 --> 45:14.066
I believe you're a fine lawyer, Ms. Minamida.

689
45:15.108 --> 45:16.777
I want to help you, Ririi.

690
45:16.860 --> 45:17.861
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
